# How many /etc/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants symlinks each package of
# this producer ships. os/tests/deb-package-gate.sh reads this and counts the
# links in the built archive.
#
# The archive cannot answer this on its own: the symlink IS the fact under
# test, so a gate that derived the expectation from the payload would assert
# that whatever shipped is what was meant. The producer states the intent here
# and the gate compares.
#
# Every package this producer emits needs a line. A package that ships no link
# says `0` rather than being left out, because an omission and a deliberate
# zero look identical and only one of them is a decision.
#
# mosd and mos-apid each own the link that starts them. Installing the package
# is what makes the daemon run; nothing calls `systemctl enable`.
mosd 1
mos-apid 1
